  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Living Ledger",
    "overview": "AmazeCC's Material 3 Expressive language treats the screen as a ledger that is quietly alive. On an absolute-black canvas, records are laid out with accounting clarity — five tonal strata, hairline separators, uppercase micro-labels — and then made tactile: cards compress under a finger, connected tabs crossfade into a selected pill with a checkmark, and the wavy progress meter gives attendance and marks a visible pulse. The system is precise and calm at rest, sculptural and optimistic in motion.\n\nColor is scarce and semantic. Periwinkle, sky, and blush are roles for primary, secondary, and tertiary actions; mint, amber, and coral carry success, caution, and error. They never decorate. Depth comes first from the tonal ladder and only then from a controlled pair of lift shadows. Type stays inside Material 3 roles, with local overrides only for the two moments that matter: the uppercase micro-label and the oversized metric.\n\nThe migration plan retires the legacy AmazeTheme/AccentTheme pill-and-glow interface and forbids amazeui, shadcn, and Tailwind web styles. Material 3 governs structure, navigation, and interaction; iOS/Cupertino controls are not part of this language, and the same design carries across the KMP targets without an OS-specific redesign. Midnight OLED and Classic Light are two first-class appearances of the same language with their own role values; neither is an inversion or a reduced version of the other.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Pitch-black, five-tier tonal canvas with hairline borders instead of generalized shadows.",
      "Spring physics on every interactive element; a 3dp sine wave is the signature meter.",
      "Sculptural asymmetric corners on stat cards, regular large radii on containers, full pills on navigation.",
      "Semantic-only color: status and selection are the only reasons an accent appears."
    ],
    "rules": [
      { "name": "The Two Appearances Rule", "body": "Midnight and Classic Light are parallel schemes with their own role values. Never derive one by inverting the other, and never let a component hard-code a value that only works in one.", "section": "colors" },
      { "name": "The Signal Rule", "body": "An accent appears only to show state, selection, or amount. A decorative accent is a bug.", "section": "colors" },
      { "name": "The Ink Rule", "body": "The canvas is pure black. Depth is earned through tonal tiers, never by tinting the background.", "section": "colors" },
      { "name": "The Two-Voice Rule", "body": "Give every number a Black-weight headline with tight tracking and every label an uppercase, wide-tracked micro-size. Everything in between stays quiet.", "section": "typography" },
      { "name": "The Tonal First Rule", "body": "If a layer can be separated with a tonal step and a hairline border, do not add a shadow.", "section": "elevation" },
      { "name": "The Asymmetry Rule", "body": "Never normalize a stat card to a uniform radius. Its uneven corners are what make the ledger feel sculptural rather than generic.", "section": "shapes" }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the five tonal tiers and a hairline border before reaching for a shadow.",
      "Do drive interaction feedback with the spring specs: spatialDefault, spatialFast, spatialSlow, and effectsDefault.",
      "Do clip dynamic text to one line with ellipsis; course codes, room names, and labels must never wrap into a card.",
      "Do collapse every spec to an instant, non-bouncy spring when the OS Reduce Motion setting or the in-app animation toggle is off.",
      "Do give clickable cards and chips an explicit button role, focus, and Enter/Space activation.",
      "Do verify every component in both Midnight and Classic Light; each appearance uses its own role tokens and neither is an afterthought."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use raw hex values in components; reference the named tokens.",
      "Don't port iOS/Cupertino controls or bring back amazeui, shadcn, or Tailwind web styles.",
      "Don't resurrect the legacy neon-glow, uniformly-pilled AmazeTheme/AccentTheme look.",
      "Don't tint the pure-black canvas or stack shadows on ordinary cards.",
      "Don't hand-pick per-screen font families or reintroduce the legacy Outfit/Geist pairing in M3E screens."
    ]
  }
}
